## Source-only RX, handshake and output-alias follow-up (2026-11-07)

Four independent DCO fixes were pushed to `main` after the stable lock
checkpoint, each with a synthetic failing regression before the change and a
passing strict C++14 and C++17 AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer
host run afterward:

- `d675ead`: `inspectStationRx` rejects broadcast, all-zero and other
  multicast Ethernet source addresses in infrastructure FromDS frames (host
  failure exit 20). An associated AP's valid BSSID is not sufficient to make
  an invalid Ethernet source safe to forward.
- `8b0c594`: WPA2-PSK EAPOL-Key traffic must use the selected associated
  BSSID as its source; ordinary MIC/PN-validated bridged data still permits
  other valid individual Ethernet sources (host failure exit 21).
- `c077bf1`: management request serializers validate writable length aliases
  against borrowed inputs even when the output packet pointer is null; the
  no-output ordinary error still clears a nonaliased count (failure exit 7).
- `c95d327`: WPA2 crypto callback outputs, including the unwrapped length,
  cannot overwrite the known starting address of the opaque hardware provider
  context. The owner must still guarantee disjointness of the context's full
  unknown allocation (failure exit 22).

Each source change was followed by a stable, default-on full
